Where do you get that information from? From wan2-343:

Magical objects (see the next section) will
tend not to polymorph into non-magical ones, and vice versa; the
probabilities of this for the object classes that have members of each
kind are as below.

class       magical -> non-magical  non-magical -> magical
~~~~~     : ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
armour    :        54%                        0.6%
gem       :        92%                      negligible
potion    :       1.7%                         41%
scroll    :     negligible                     92%
spellbook :     negligible                     95%
tool      :        60%                        0.3%
wand      :     negligible                     93%


While it is true that nonmagical armor, tools and gems will rarely 
polypile into magical objects, the same is not true of all object types.


